{"name":"Dried Palm","hex":"#e1dbac","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dried","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without water or moisture, said of something that has previously been wet or moist; resulting from the process of drying.","Usually of foods: cured, preserved by drying."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of dry"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dried"},{"term":"palm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various evergreen trees from the family Palmae or Arecaceae, which are mainly found in the tropics.","A branch or leaf of the palm, anciently borne or worn as a symbol of victory or rejoicing."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The inner and somewhat concave part of the human hand or other primate hand that extends from the wrist to the bases of the fingers.","The corresponding part of the forefoot of a nonprimate mammal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palm"}],"entries":[],"images":[],"sounds":{"dried":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1a/En-us-dried.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/1a/En-us-dried.ogg/En-us-dried.ogg.mp3"}],"palm":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/46/En-us-palm.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/46/En-us-palm.ogg/En-us-palm.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Beige Chromography","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/38/Beige_Chromography.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":1,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beige_Chromography.jpg","share":0.390625},{"title":"Bl